// Title: x-typecheck-patterns-02 variant: an abstract pattern nested in a tuple, struct or
//   slice over a union of two instantiations binds its payload at ONE member's type.
// Command: timeout -s KILL 20 graphix --no-cache x-rerun-2-nested-abstract-bind-one-member.gx
//          (and --no-fusion; and --check of the `let q: string = b` form in the CR)
// Expected: `b` is typed [bool, i64] (the union of its part of every member the arm can
//   match, as `Box(b)` at top level and `A(Box(b)) inside a variant are), so `b + 1` is
//   refused; without the `_` arm the select is exhaustive, as the top-level form is.
// Observed: the check types `b` as i64 (`let q: string = b` reports "string does not
//   contain i64" for the tuple, the struct field and the slice head alike), so `b + 1`
//   is accepted. Node-walk prints 1 for h((Box(false), 1)); the JIT panics
//   "kernel param `b`: runtime Bool(false) does not match the compiled Scalar(I64) slot"
//   and the runtime dies ("Error: runtime did not respond"). Without `_ => 0` the check
//   refuses "no arm covers ([Box<i64>, Box<bool>], i64)".
type Box<'a> = Abstract<'a>;
let h = |x: ([Box<bool>, Box<i64>], i64)| select x { (Box(b), n) => b + 1, _ => 0 };
sys::exit(sys::time::after_idle(duration:100.ms, 0));
h((Box(false), 1))
